<h1>Settings</h1>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Account</h2>
  <p class="dim">Signed in as <%= user.email %>. Ask whoever runs your club if that needs to change.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Letterboxd</h2>
  <p>We read this account's public watchlist once a week to work out what everyone wants to see.</p>
  <% if error %><p class="err"><%= error %></p><% end %>
  <form method="post" action="/settings">
    <%== csrf_tag("/settings") %>
    <p><input type="text" name="letterboxd_username" value="<%= username %>"
              placeholder="username" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off" spellcheck="false"></p>
    <p class="dim">
      Username only &mdash; not the full URL, though we'll cope. Your watchlist has to be public.
      <%# Said plainly here rather than behind a confirm: it's recoverable
          (change it back and the next crawl fills it in again), but somebody
          swapping accounts should know their votes-in-waiting go with it. %>
      Changing this drops the watchlist we hold for you and reads the new
      account's instead.
    </p>
    <button type="submit">Save</button>
  </form>
</section>
